From 95e0f6400a7e9cf9782fb0efeb0cfbe9f1ac16ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Freeze hub claim lanes before admission to exclude
 asynchronous wakes

Problem: t_01a18e12cdcab970 woke stale at 1794610055 and was claimed
on the hub at 1794610056 with no hub_admission event.
Why 1: the claim pass enumerated ready rows after the admission screen.
Why 2: wake probes publish ready/review from separate connections while
screening runs (kanban_wake_check._probe_and_apply/apply_result/_wake).
Why 3: admission screened an earlier candidate snapshot, not the set
subsequently enumerated for claims (dispatch worker_pickup -> lane_rows).
Root (happened): two independently sampled candidate sets straddled an
asynchronous producer; resumable review cards were also outside the screen.
Root (not caught): claim-screen fixtures started ready; wake tests exercised
promotion but not a completion between admission and claim enumeration.
Recurrence: extends PR #1637; its row/event fence protects verdict application,
not newly arrived candidates. The prior fence remains unchanged.

Freeze both lanes after foreign pickup and before the existing screen.
Late wakes wait one tick; the next screen judges, moves, keeps or fails open
under the existing policy. Include review resumptions in admission.

Proof: ready race RED (red-run2, hub holder without verdict), then GREEN.
Review race RED before frozen review snapshot and again before review screen
inclusion; GREEN afterwards. Added real wake result/timer matrix covering
ready/review and existing verdicts. Focused four suites green-run3 rc=0;
scripts/check --base origin/main check-run2 rc=0.

Remaining pre-publication work: final-byte tests/mutations, live predicate
replay, watch count reconciliation and independent exact-head review/CI.
